      "text_blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "snippet": "A Roth IRA can still make sense at any age, even in retirement, but it may be less advantageous for those who expect to be in a lower tax bracket in retirement and have limited time to allow for tax-free growth. If you are older and expect to have lower income in retirement, a traditional IRA might be a better option because you can deduct contributions now and pay taxes on withdrawals later when your tax rate is potentially lower. However, a Roth IRA still offers benefits like tax-free growth and the absence of required minimum distributions (RMDs), which can be valuable regardless of age.",
